PR #1033 should fix this. There was a problem with the `lang_start` intrinsic, which overrides the stdlib entry point. Until the fix is merged one can use this workaround which defines a custom entry point (only available on the nightly channel):

```Rust
#![feature(start)]
#![feature(termination_trait_lib)]
use std::{
    process::Termination,
    panic,
};

#[start]
#[no_mangle]
fn start(_argc : isize, _argv : *const *const u8) -> isize {
    panic::catch_unwind(|| main().report()).unwrap_or(101) as isize
}

fn main() {
    println!("Hello Rust!")
}
